Review round for the 0.2.1 patch release. Five independent agents read
3f51087, one for each declared review. Each received its criteria, the
diff and the repository path, and nothing from the driver's thread. All
five verdicts are PASS.

Every reviewer recorded the same window: three of the four install
commands in the README do not resolve until the tag publishes them.
That ordering is forced. The README is the registry description, so it
has to read correctly inside the tagged tree, and the tag cannot exist
before the commit that carries it. A source-build command sits in the
same section as recovery.

